      entry_price: number;
      strike?: number | null;
      entry_iv?: number | null;
      strategy_id?: string | null;
      expiration_date?: string | null;
      stop_loss_price?: number | null;
      take_profit_price?: number | null;
    }>,
  ) => {
```

Nothing else changes — the insert mapping's `leg.strike ?? null` lines stay as the single normalization point before data hits Supabase. All five call sites (market order, pending trigger, option order, strategy legs) now flow through without friction, and future callers won't trip on the same wire.

*(The alternative — rewriting `resolvedLegs` to produce `undefined`s — would work but fights the domain: SQL has no "missing column," only NULL. When forced to choose conventions at a boundary, match the boundary.)*

